------------------------------------
BLOCK ANALYSIS FOR ERROR ESTIMATION
-----------------------------------
This directory contains scripts to perform block analysis on Metadynamics data. 


## REQUIRED FILES:

	- colvar_weighted file from step 2
	- find_block_dim.sh
	- do_block_fes_v2.py
	- plot_block_err.py

## BLOCK ANALYSIS
#Compute error ad function of block size

Inspect the plot hills height vs time from the preliminary analysis to select the equilibration time.
Customize parameters in find_block_dim.sh if necessary. Defaults:
	- MIN_BSIZE=10
	- NUM_POINTS=50
	- BIN_RESOLUTION=0.05
	- ORIGINAL_MASTER="colvar_weighted"
	- W_NAME="weight"  
	- KBT=2.477710

Run:
module load python

./find_block_dim.sh <CV_NAME> <EQUIL_TIME>

<CV_NAME>: name of the collective variable column in your colvar file (e.g., armsdC).

<EQUIL_TIME>: amount of time (in ps) to discard as equilibration (e.g., 400000).

# OUTPUT

	-   block_analysis_{CV} --> directory containing the FES output for each block size and a summary file named err.blocks

# Plot the error vs. block dimension
From the block_analysis_{CV} folder

python ../plot_block_err.py -f err.blocks -o err_{CV}.png --title {CV} Block Error"

## OUTPUT

	- err_{CV}.png --> plot showing the average FES error (in kcal/mol) on the y-axis versus the block size on the x-axis. The optimal block size to report is where the curve flattens out.

This script was developed following the PLUMED MASTERCLASS and the do_block_fes_v2.py script is a modified verision of do_block_fes.py from M. Bonomi.
https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.7/user-doc/html/masterclass-21-1.html
https://github.com/plumed/masterclass-21-4
